#: gui/main.c:3007
msgid ""
"How the list of files shows each one: its name, then on the right its state and its size.\r\n"
"    No state: a good copy is on a drive that is plugged in.\r\n"
"    On <drive>, name in grey: its copy is on a drive that is not plugged in.\r\n"
"    Not backed up, name in grey italics: it has no copy yet.\r\n"
"    Changed since backup: only an older version is backed up.\r\n"
"    Copy damaged: the copy on the plugged-in drive is missing or damaged; back up again to fix it.\r\n"
"    Deleted, name struck through: gone from its folder; BRODALF still keeps track of its copies.\r\n"
"    May be damaged: a bit-rot scan found it changed without its size or time changing (Damaged files...).\r\n"
"    3 of 10 available, on a folder: how many files in it have a good copy on a plugged-in drive.\r\n"
"    ★ after a name: starred, also copied to your extra places. A lock: encrypted on every drive and extra place it is copied to.\r\n"
"    Point at a name for all of this in words. A file's versions are in its details."
msgstr ""

